    "body": "The rendered ground could sit 1.50 m below the shared gameplay height at the watchtower, and the river disappeared under terrain at 26% of sampled wet positions. This disconnect undermined foot planting, scenery contact and the continuity of the landscape.\n\nThis change replaces the coarse separate terrain grids with one stitched adaptive surface, preserves the exact five landmark anchors, follows the actual river bed with a shallow bounded flowing sheet, folds wet banks into the ground material, corrects backface bump orientation, and stabilizes the sun shadow grid. Collision, saves, placement, title video and audio remain on the current gameplay contracts.\n\nValidation: all 17 local gate commands and 223 tests passed in 88.166 s. Independent actual-index geometry comparison on the same 555,901 points reduced maximum contact error from 1.502110 m to 0.059330 m; a denser separate sample family remains below 0.10 m. Hidden water samples fell 7,740→0 of the same 29,756 wet points, including the maximum negative wave. No terrain holes or topology failures. Initial JS stays 163,175 B under the existing 165,000 B gate; standalone 13,120,704 B is byte-verified against the stage.\n\nThe remote tree matches the locally validated tree 3fe6bfcde2ecfb26b5d4f3951ae9e3271f5b7a40 exactly. Required CI must pass before normal merge. Official preview infrastructure is unavailable, so this does not claim WebGL, real-device/FPS, physical touch, audio listening, or PS4 perceptual parity. This is one finite production unit; foliage, continuous actor motion and actual-weapon VFX continue separately.",
